{"id": "kv.flush.not.implemented", "op": "flush", "version": 1, "args": {}, "want": {"error_contains": "op Flush not implemented"}, "note": "Op::Flush is defined in skeg-proto but unimplemented server-side", "wire_only": "the SDK exposes no method for an op the server does not implement; validate_native.py covers it"}
{"id": "admission.setup.index", "op": "vindex_create", "version": 1, "args": {"name": "cfnadm", "dim": 4, "kind": 0, "backend": 0}, "want": {"op": "ok"}}
{"id": "admission.dim.mismatch.is.permanent", "op": "vset", "version": 1, "args": {"name": "cfnadm", "id": 1, "vector": [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]}, "want": {"error_code": 2, "retryable": false}, "note": "the same control row as the RESP3 case of this name: one classification, two wires"}
{"id": "admission.frame.over.allowance.is.refused.by.name", "op": "ping", "version": 1, "args": {}, "declared_payload_len": 33554432, "want": {"error_code": 2, "retryable": false, "error_contains": "at most"}, "note": "a header declaring more than the connection may ever hold; the server used to close the socket without a word, which a client reads as a network fault and answers by reconnecting and sending it again", "wire_only": "a hand-built header whose declared length does not match its body; validate_native.py covers it"}
